       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use. At that dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common regimen for inflammatory conditions\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum dose\n- **1600 mg/day total**, divided differently\n\nIf 1600 mg four times daily is what you want, tell me and add a note with the clinical rationale. I'll then enter it as written. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
